multiview-stage2.patch — advertise GL_OVR_multiview/2 in the ANGLE Metal backend
==========================================================================
(stage 2 of the multiview plan of the Vice City port)

Base:        ANGLE e4499e6b2835a6996507f1b99920bc56f0122573
Order:       apply after klepton.patch AND angle-metal-fixes.patch.
State:       stage 2 COMPLETE (2026-09-23) — the extension is advertised,
             STILL WITHOUT EFFECT: the guest sees GL_OVR_multiview/multiview2
             and MAX_VIEWS_OVR=2, draws still land in one eye.
             Part 2 (accepting a multiview attachment) needed NO backend
             change: glFramebufferTextureMultiviewOVR on a 64x64x2 array
             with two views returns COMPLETE without a GL error (guest
             self-test in visionos_angle.mm, device 2026-09-23) —
             FramebufferMtl/TextureMtl handle the 2DArrayRange index out of
             the box (render target = base layer). This patch therefore
             stays the announcement only; stage 3+ (gl_ViewID_OVR in the
             shader) follows separately.

Activation:  ONLY with the environment variable KL_GL_MULTIVIEW=1 (default:
             off — without the variable the extension string does not
             change). Verified on the device 2026-09-23 (guest sees both
             extensions active, MAX_VIEWS_OVR=2, game unaffected).

diff --git a/src/libANGLE/renderer/metal/DisplayMtl.mm b/src/libANGLE/renderer/metal/DisplayMtl.mm
index dbc9481363..10fcef1a3c 100644
--- a/src/libANGLE/renderer/metal/DisplayMtl.mm
+++ b/src/libANGLE/renderer/metal/DisplayMtl.mm
@@ -721,6 +721,14 @@ bool IsMetalDisplayAvailable()
     initializeExtensions();
     initializeTextureCaps();
 
+    // VC multiview, Stufe 2: the cap belonging to OVR_multiview above. Two is
+    // both the stereo need and the device's rate-map layer maximum (measured,
+    // see multiview-plan.md Stufe 0).
+    if (mNativeExtensions.multiviewOVR)
+    {
+        mNativeCaps.maxViews = 2;
+    }
+
     // https://developer.apple.com/metal/Metal-Feature-Set-Tables.pdf
     mNativeCaps.maxElementIndex  = std::numeric_limits<GLuint>::max() - 1;
     mNativeCaps.max3DTextureSize = 2048;
@@ -967,6 +975,22 @@ bool IsMetalDisplayAvailable()
     // only source of YUV textures is the EGLImage sibling over a decoder frame.
     mNativeExtensions.yuvInternalFormatANGLE        = true;
 
+    // VC multiview, Stufe 2 (Docs/vicecity/multiview-plan.md): advertise
+    // GL_OVR_multiview/2 to the guest WITHOUT any backend effect yet — draws
+    // still land single-eyed. Gated by KL_GL_MULTIVIEW=1 (default OFF) so the
+    // extension string only changes when the experiment explicitly asks for
+    // it; the frontend validation and entry points are generic and already
+    // compiled in. maxViews is set alongside in ensureCapsInitialized.
+    static const bool klMultiview = [] {
+        const char *e = getenv("KL_GL_MULTIVIEW");
+        return e && e[0] == '1';
+    }();
+    if (klMultiview)
+    {
+        mNativeExtensions.multiviewOVR  = true;
+        mNativeExtensions.multiview2OVR = true;
+    }
+
     // EXT_debug_marker is not implemented yet, but the entry points must be exposed for the
     // Metal backend to be used in Chrome (http://anglebug.com/42263519)
     mNativeExtensions.debugMarkerEXT = true;
